  (938, 'MFR-20', 20, 1, NULL, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.2REBAZODI&productId=13509', 'ADVERSARIALLY VERIFIED 2026-07-24: independently re-fetched https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.2REBAZODI&productId=13509 via curl and read live table text. CONFIRMED: ''Density, maximum (du/ac): n/a [Single-Family/Duplex] / 20 du/ac [Multifamily] / 20 du/ac [Duplex Subdivisions] / 20 du/ac [Townhouse Subdivisions] / n/a [Nonresidential]'' and ''Floor area ratio (FAR), maximum: n/a / n/a / n/a / n/a / 1.0 [Nonresidential Development]'' -- exact match to researcher''s reported max_density_du_acre=20 and max_far=1.0. Daytona Beach LDC Sec. 4.2.D (Multifamily Residential-20). Ordinance table explicitly states ''Density, maximum (du/ac): 20 du/ac'' for the Multifamily/Duplex-Subdivision/Townhouse-Subdivision columns (district''s characteristic use is multifamily per its purpose statement) -- used directly. far_applicable=true, max_far=1.0 taken directly f', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (938, 'RP', NULL, 1, 3.5, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.2REBAZODI&productId=13509', 'PARTIALLY spot-checked as a byproduct of fetching the same Sec 4.2 document for SFR-5/MFR-20 verification (not one of the formal top-2 targets). Live table CONFIRMS max_far=1.0 (Nonresidential Development column) and density showing ''n/a'' for single-family/nonresidential with ''20 du/ac'' for multifamily/duplex-sub/townhouse-sub columns, consistent with researcher''s description. parking_per_1000sf=3.5 NOT independently verified (would require checking Table 6.2.C.1 in Article 6, not in the fetched Sec 4.2 document). Daytona Beach LDC Sec. 4.2.F (Residential/Professional R/P). Ordinance table shows density varying by unit-type sub-column within the same district: single-family/duplex = n/a (lot-size governed), multifamily/duplex-subdivision/townhouse-subdivision = 20 du/ac each, nonresidential = n/a. Per campaign rule this is a lot-size-varies-by-unit-type table, not a single per-acre figur', 0.7, '2026-07-24'),
  (938, 'RDD2', 40, 10, NULL, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.7REBAZODI&productId=13509', 'NOT independently re-verified this session. Daytona Beach LDC Sec. 4.7.O (Redevelopment Downtown - Central Business District, coded ''RDD-2'' in the ordinance -- our GIS data''s ''RDD2'' is the same code without the hyphen, confidence 0.9 for this direct textual match). Ordinance table explicitly states ''Density, maximum: 40 du/ac'' and ''Floor area ratio (FAR), maximum: 10.0'' -- both used directly. pk1000_applicable=false: Sec. 4.7.O.4.a Modified Development Standards explicitly states ''Off-street parking is required for residential uses only'' for this district -- nonresidential/commercial uses in RDD-2 are exempt from off-street parking entirely, so there is no per-1,000sf ratio to report (not a gap, a genuine zero-requirement finding).', 0.9, '2026-07-24'),
  (938, 'MFR-40', 40, NULL, NULL, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.2REBAZODI&productId=13509', 'NOT independently re-verified this session (outside top-2 by likely parcel count -- MFR-40 is typically a smaller oceanfront-strip zone, less common than SFR-5/MFR-20). Daytona Beach LDC Sec. 4.2.E (Multifamily Residential-40). Ordinance table explicitly states ''Density, maximum (du/ac): 40 du/ac'' for the Multifamily/Duplex-Subdivision/Townhouse-Subdivision columns (district''s characteristic use is high-density multifamily per its purpose statement) -- used directly. far_applicable=false: unlike MFR-20, the MFR-40 table''s ''Nonresidential Development'' FAR cell reads ''n/a'' (confirmed by direct read of the ordinance table -- MFR-40 genuinely does not permit/regulate nonresidential FAR the way MFR-20 does). pk1000_applicable=false: residential parking here is per-unit (''2 per du'' for multifamily dwelling, Table 6.2.C.1), not per-1,000sf.', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (938, 'RDM6', 8, NULL, NULL, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=492952&nodeId=DABELADECO_ART4ZODI_S4.7REBAZODI&productId=13509', 'NOT independently re-verified this session. Daytona Beach LDC Sec. 4.7.Z (Redevelopment Midtown - Residential Preservation, coded ''RDM-6'' in the ordinance -- our GIS data''s ''RDM6'' is the same code without the hyphen, confidence 0.9 for this direct textual match). Ordinance table states ''Density, maximum: n/a'' for the Single-Family Residential column but explicitly ''8 du/ac'' for the ''Other Residential Development'' column -- used directly per the explicit-stated-number rule (this is the district''s non-single-family residential track; single-family remains lot-size-governed at 5,000 sf min but that figure is identical between the two columns so 8 du/ac is reported as the district''s meaningful multi-unit cap). far_applicable=false: table shows FAR ''n/a'' for both Single-Family and Other Residential Development columns -- confirmed genuine non-applicability, not a gap. pk1000_applicable=false:', 0.9, '2026-07-24'),
  (885, 'R-3M', 12, NULL, NULL, 'https://library.municode.com/fl/port_orange/codes/land_development_code?nodeId=LADECO_CH17ZODIRE_S12MODEMUREDI', 'VERIFIED via direct Municode backend API fetch (api.municode.com/CodesContent, ClientID 3932, productId 12297) bypassing the blocked library.municode.com JS shell. Sec.12(b)(1) text reads verbatim: ''Multifamily dwellings (12 units per gross acre maximum allowable density).'' Sec.27 table confirmed to show conflicting sub-row data (row H unified-ownership = dash; row i fee-simple = 2,000 sq.ft./D.U. = 21.78 du/acre) -- researcher correctly used the explicit Sec.12 stated cap of 12 rather than back-calculating. No FAR anywhere in Ch.17 confirmed. Original researcher note fully accurate.', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (885, 'R-8SF', 5.445, NULL, NULL, 'https://library.municode.com/fl/port_orange/codes/land_development_code?nodeId=LADECO_CH17ZODIRE_S27SCDIRE', 'VERIFIED via direct Municode backend API fetch (api.municode.com/CodesContent, ClientID 3932, productId 12297). Sec.27 Schedule of Dimensional Requirements table row for R-8SF confirmed: Minimum Lot Area/D.U. = ''8,000 sq. ft.'', Minimum Lot Width = 80 ft. 43,560/8,000 = 5.445 du/acre matches exactly. Original researcher note fully accurate.', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (885, 'RMH', 5.808, NULL, NULL, 'https://library.municode.com/fl/port_orange/codes/land_development_code?nodeId=LADECO_CH17ZODIRE_S16MOHORERMDI', 'Not independently re-verified this pass (spot-check budget spent on R-8SF/R-10SF/R-3M/RD). Original note internally consistent with the verified Sec.27 table structure (7,500 sq ft matches the pattern seen for R-7SF row). Left unchanged.', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (885, 'RD', 16, NULL, 5, 'https://library.municode.com/fl/port_orange/codes/land_development_code?nodeId=LADECO_CH17ZODIRE_S25RIDERDDI', 'VERIFIED via direct Municode backend API fetch (api.municode.com/CodesContent, ClientID 3932, productId 12297). Sec.25(b)(9) text reads verbatim: ''Multifamily dwellings (16 units per gross acre maximum allowable density) (subsection 14).'' Confirmed this is a special-exception use, not the district''s base use. Sec.25(a) purpose/intent confirmed verbatim: ''designed to encourage development... a mixture of office, commercial, warehouse/storage, and limited industrial uses.'' Sec.27 table row for RD shows Minimum Living Area/D.U.=dash and Minimum Lot Area/D.U.=''10,000 sq. ft.'' with footnote B, and footnote B is confirmed to read ''Minimum lot width and area apply to newly created lots'' -- i.e. a general lot-subdivision minimum, NOT a per-dwelling-unit density figure, which supports (does not contradict) the researcher''s claim that RD''s base table carries no residential density metric. Parking ', 0.7, '2026-07-24'),
