  (1135, 'R-2', 4.356, NULL, NULL, 'https://www.cityofedgewater.org/DocumentCenter/View/809 (Edgewater LDC Article V, Table V-1 Site Dimensions, 2024-O-34)', 'VERIFIED via independent re-fetch (curl+pdftotext -layout on the actual PDF, since it is a non-OCR-friendly scanned/vector doc that pypdf/WebFetch could not read directly). Table V-1 row confirmed verbatim: ''R-2, Single Family Residential (13) 10,000 80 125 30 20 10 26 30 60 1,200'' = min lot area 10,000 sq ft, matching researcher''s claim exactly. Footnote (13) only concerns SR 442 setback, does not affect lot area. 43,560/10,000 = 4.356 du/acre confirmed. Table''s last column is labeled ''Min. Floor Area Sq. Ft.'' (a per-unit minimum size requirement), not FAR -- confirmed no FAR concept exists anywhere in Table V-1 for any district. far_applicable=false and pk1000_applicable=false both correct as claimed.', 1, '2026-07-24'),
  (911, 'PUD', 18, NULL, NULL, 'https://api.municode.com/CodesContent?jobId=486114&nodeId=PTIIILADERE_ARTVZODI&productId=11341 (New Smyrna Beach LDR, Sec. 504.02, PUD Planned Unit Development district, subsection ''Density'')', 'VERIFIED via independent re-fetch (direct curl with browser User-Agent against the Municode API, which returned the full 875KB Article V content -- WebFetch alone got 403/ECONNRESET on this domain repeatedly). Located the PUD section''s exact ''Density'' subsection text: ''The maximum residential density allowed in a PUD is 18 units per acre on the mainland and 12 units per acre on beachside.'' -- word-for-word match to researcher''s citation and figure. Also independently corroborated by a separate public NSB staff-report PDF found via web search referencing ''the otherwise allowable 18 units per acre'' for PUD rezonings. Searched the entire Article V text for ''Floor Area Ratio''/''FAR'' -- zero matches anywhere in the district regulations chapter, confirming far_applicable=false is correct (a FAR figure mentioned in one search result was a project-specific negotiated PUD condition, not a base-cod', 1, '2026-07-24'),
